@call c02 fall_cardiac start=09:41:30
@patient age=78 sex=female weight_kg=60 complaint="fall, felt lightheaded and heart racing before falling" allergies=penicillin home_meds="Eliquis, metoprolol" history="atrial fibrillation"
@traps atrial fibrillation with RVR; afib
RD: Medic 7, fall, seventy-eight year old female, lift assist requested.  >> dispatch:fall, lift assist "fall, seventy-eight year old female, lift assist"
GAP 3
M2: On scene, Medic 7.  >> time:eTimes.06 "On scene"
GAP 3
BY: She's in the kitchen, she went down about twenty minutes ago.
M1: Ma'am, did you trip, or did you feel funny before you fell?
PT: I got dizzy, my heart was going so fast, and then I was on the floor.
M1: Did you hit your head? Are you on blood thinners?
PT: I don't think so. I take Eliquis and metoprolol. I'm allergic to penicillin.
M1: Okay. Found her on the floor, alert, no obvious injury, but this isn't just a fall.  >> found:on the floor, lightheaded, palpitations "Found her on the floor"
TAP knock +label
M2: Heart rate's 148 and irregular, BP 96 over 60, sat 93.  >> vital:hr=148 "Heart rate's 148"; vital:bp=96/60 "BP 96 over 60"; vital:spo2=93 "sat 93"
GAP 4
M1: Get the monitor on her and a twelve lead.  >> proc:12-lead ECG "twelve lead"
GAP 10
TAP button -
GAP 12
M2: She's a GCS 15, A and O times four.  >> status:A&O×4 "A and O times four"; vital:gcs=15 "GCS 15"
GAP 3
TAP snap +label
M2: Twenty in the right hand.  >> proc:IV access "Twenty in the right hand"
M1: Start 500 of saline, wide open.  >> med:normal saline,500,, "500 of saline"
GAP 6
M1: Blood sugar's 112.  >> vital:bgl=112 "Blood sugar's 112"
GAP 5
M1: Let's go, we're transporting to General.  >> time:eTimes.09 "we're transporting"
GAP 8
TAP button +label
M2: Recheck, 104 over 66, rate 132.  >> vital:bp=104/66 "104 over 66"; vital:hr=132 "rate 132"
GAP 12
M1: At General now.  >> time:eTimes.11 "At General now"
GAP 6
TAP knock +label
M1: Report's given, transfer of care complete.  >> time:eTimes.12 "transfer of care complete"
